WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:02.128
- Friday nights in high school,

00:00:02.128 --> 00:00:03.299
my friends would go out,

00:00:03.299 --> 00:00:04.132
they would make out,

00:00:04.132 --> 00:00:04.965
they would go to the movies,

00:00:04.965 --> 00:00:06.024
they would go to the malls.

00:00:06.024 --> 00:00:09.208
I had to go to church, this a true story!

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:14.139
(swish and creaking)
(upbeat drum music)

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:16.622
- First of all, we weren't
allowed to go to any sleepovers.

00:00:16.622 --> 00:00:18.114
- Sleepovers were a no.

00:00:18.114 --> 00:00:18.994
- They were insulted.

00:00:18.994 --> 00:00:19.827
They're like,

00:00:19.827 --> 00:00:21.007
"Why would you want to sleep
at someone else's house?"

00:00:21.007 --> 00:00:23.436
"Someone might touch you,
or like, abduct you."

00:00:23.436 --> 00:00:24.269
- "I didn't work hard

00:00:24.269 --> 00:00:25.967
for you to sleep at somebody else's house,

00:00:25.967 --> 00:00:26.826
you gon' sleep right here."

00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:29.133
- I wanted to paint my nails
and talk about cute boys,

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:30.255
and like, my parents were like,

00:00:30.255 --> 00:00:32.316
"Hell no, they can come sleep over here"

00:00:32.316 --> 00:00:33.743
"You can't go to their house"

00:00:33.743 --> 00:00:35.287
- I'm still friends with my friends,

00:00:35.287 --> 00:00:36.665
and their parents are great.

00:00:36.665 --> 00:00:39.196
I guess my parents just
didn't fully know that,

00:00:39.196 --> 00:00:40.767
coming from a different country,

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:42.996
it's hard to trust
people who you don't know

00:00:42.996 --> 00:00:44.079
from like day one.

00:00:44.079 --> 00:00:46.579
- I'm Egyptian, was raised Muslim,

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.484
and in my household that
meant that we couldn't wear

00:00:48.484 --> 00:00:50.159
anything that was provocative.

00:00:50.159 --> 00:00:52.542
Nothing low cut, no short shorts,

00:00:52.542 --> 00:00:55.332
and nothing that showed
off your midriff at all.

00:00:55.332 --> 00:00:58.443
- We had to have Indian food
for dinner, no matter what.

00:00:58.443 --> 00:00:59.532
We didn't go like McDonald's.

00:00:59.532 --> 00:01:01.617
We didn't go get like fast food at all.

00:01:01.617 --> 00:01:03.795
- My mom got really confused
by after school clubs.

00:01:03.795 --> 00:01:05.654
She thought it was the same as clubbing,

00:01:05.654 --> 00:01:07.915
so she was very strict on
like which ones I'd join,

00:01:07.915 --> 00:01:10.023
and was like, "You're too
young to go clubbing!"

00:01:10.023 --> 00:01:12.216
And I'm like, "Mom, that's
not the same thing."

00:01:12.216 --> 00:01:13.926
- We can't leave the
house until we're married.

00:01:13.926 --> 00:01:16.406
That even kind of went into
us kind of going to college,

00:01:16.406 --> 00:01:19.275
we couldn't go to colleges
very far or even apply.

00:01:19.275 --> 00:01:21.931
- I was not allowed to
celebrate Halloween.

00:01:21.931 --> 00:01:24.821
My parents said that Halloween
was the Devil's birthday.

00:01:24.821 --> 00:01:28.126
And that I was not able
to dress up in costumes

00:01:28.126 --> 00:01:29.136
'cause it was a sin.

00:01:29.136 --> 00:01:31.731
But anyway, I basically had
to make this book report

00:01:31.731 --> 00:01:34.074
and convince my parents that Halloween

00:01:34.074 --> 00:01:36.236
is not a sinful holiday to celebrate.

00:01:36.236 --> 00:01:38.294
And then I, thankfully got to celebrate it

00:01:38.294 --> 00:01:39.127
for the rest of my life.

00:01:39.127 --> 00:01:40.312
- It was more around grades,

00:01:40.312 --> 00:01:41.661
you know they wanted straight A's,

00:01:41.661 --> 00:01:43.481
that's who they were.

00:01:43.481 --> 00:01:44.640
Gotta greet your parents,

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:45.952
gotta greet all elders.

00:01:45.952 --> 00:01:47.341
Super important.

00:01:47.341 --> 00:01:49.803
That's probably like one of
the most important things.

00:01:49.803 --> 00:01:51.301
- Cleaning a lot.

00:01:51.301 --> 00:01:53.853
We were responsible for
making our bed every morning.

00:01:53.853 --> 00:01:55.213
We weren't allowed to sleep in.

00:01:55.213 --> 00:01:56.611
I don't understand why.

00:01:56.611 --> 00:01:58.213
Let a kid sleep, please!

00:01:58.213 --> 00:02:00.141
- Well first, we couldn't drink soda.

00:02:00.141 --> 00:02:01.733
I mean, we could eat sweets, but like,

00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:03.653
when she would pack our lunches,

00:02:03.653 --> 00:02:05.453
she would only put one sweet thing

00:02:05.453 --> 00:02:07.872
and it had to only be the serving size

00:02:07.872 --> 00:02:09.032
of the sweet thing.

00:02:09.032 --> 00:02:11.501
So if it said like half a
cookie was a serving size,

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:13.611
you know my mom is
giving us half a cookie.

00:02:13.611 --> 00:02:16.373
- In my early childhood,
I grew up in New York, so

00:02:16.373 --> 00:02:17.785
I had to make sure I was home

00:02:17.785 --> 00:02:19.735
by the time the streetlights were on.

00:02:19.735 --> 00:02:21.076
If my friends drove,

00:02:21.076 --> 00:02:23.345
I wasn't allowed to go
in the car with them.

00:02:23.345 --> 00:02:25.116
My dad didn't trust their driving skills,

00:02:25.116 --> 00:02:26.447
'cause they were brand new.

00:02:26.447 --> 00:02:28.310
That stuff was just a little bit much.

00:02:28.310 --> 00:02:30.087
- I think they could've relaxed a lot,

00:02:30.087 --> 00:02:31.817
especially when it came to curfew.

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:33.407
I would be five minutes late,

00:02:33.407 --> 00:02:35.862
and then I would get
grounded for two weeks!

00:02:35.862 --> 00:02:37.177
That ain't right!

00:02:37.177 --> 00:02:39.664
- A lot of it went back
to how hard my mom worked

00:02:39.664 --> 00:02:40.676
when she was a child,

00:02:40.676 --> 00:02:42.137
which like is incredible.

00:02:42.137 --> 00:02:45.897
But as like a child in a
different circumstance,

00:02:45.897 --> 00:02:47.647
it was very hard to understand.

00:02:47.647 --> 00:02:48.480
- I get it.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.177
I also get that my parents
were really doing their best

00:02:52.177 --> 00:02:54.967
to kind of enforce their culture,

00:02:54.967 --> 00:02:55.817
which is difficult

00:02:55.817 --> 00:02:57.537
when your kid is growing up

00:02:57.537 --> 00:02:59.297
in an entirely different country;

00:02:59.297 --> 00:03:01.065
in an entirely different space.

00:03:01.065 --> 00:03:02.407
- There's a lot of
harassment that takes place

00:03:02.407 --> 00:03:03.465
if you're a woman in India.

00:03:03.465 --> 00:03:05.079
I've been through it personally,

00:03:05.079 --> 00:03:06.481
when you're kind of exposed to that,

00:03:06.481 --> 00:03:08.647
I guess you're going to be
a little more protective

00:03:08.647 --> 00:03:09.480
of your daughters.

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.097
- Growing up in a strict household

00:03:11.097 --> 00:03:12.905
helped me to stay very focused.

00:03:12.905 --> 00:03:15.025
It kind of made me
realize what's important,

00:03:15.025 --> 00:03:16.022
which is family.

00:03:16.022 --> 00:03:18.385
- My parents had the
foresight to make sure

00:03:18.385 --> 00:03:20.345
I was good and I made it to this age,

00:03:20.345 --> 00:03:21.755
so you know, shout out to them!

00:03:21.755 --> 00:03:24.596
- They wanted us to be
close to our culture

00:03:24.596 --> 00:03:27.297
because we're so far away
from like our homeland.

00:03:27.297 --> 00:03:29.834
My ethnicity and my
identity as an Armenian

00:03:29.834 --> 00:03:32.116
is like very strong because of that,

00:03:32.116 --> 00:03:33.445
and I really appreciate that,

00:03:33.445 --> 00:03:34.278
and at the time,

00:03:34.278 --> 00:03:35.111
I know I didn't.

00:03:35.111 --> 00:03:37.747
- Let your kids figure some stuff out, but

00:03:37.747 --> 00:03:40.384
make sure they're home by the
time the streetlights come on.

00:03:40.384 --> 00:03:41.217
That's how I feel.

00:03:41.217 --> 00:03:44.300
(light upbeat music)

